#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179582 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179720 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c91d51f-39b4-547a-971b-9c2dada9eb47" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Simple Sums Over Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/id #uuid "2574b91a-6534-562b-b4dc-8d95fd19e169" :question/math-academy-id "e-9480" :question/problem "Let $P= \\left\\{y_0, y_1, \\ldots, y_n\\right\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[-3, 5].$ If $\\Delta y_j = y_j - y_{j-1},$ calculate $\\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^n {3}\\Delta y_j.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the factor $3$ outside the summation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}3Δ{y}_{j}=3{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $\\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^n \\Delta y_j$ is just the length of the interval $[-3, 5],$ because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j} & =Δ{y}_{1}+Δ{y}_{2}+Δ{y}_{3}+⋯+Δ{y}_{n} \\\\  & =({y}_{1}-{y}_{0})+({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})+({y}_{3}-{y}_{2})+⋯+({y}_{n}-{y}_{n-1}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{y}_{1}}-{y}_{0})+(\\cancel{{y}_{2}}-\\cancel{{y}_{1}})+(\\cancel{{y}_{3}}-\\cancel{{y}_{2}})+⋯+({y}_{n}-\\cancel{{y}_{n-1}}) \\\\  & =-{y}_{0}+{y}_{n} \\\\  & ={y}_{n}-{y}_{0} \\\\  & =5-(-3) \\\\  & =5+3 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{3}\\sum_{j=1}^n \\Delta y_j = 3 \\cdot 8 = 24.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179583 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179721 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f55bdc9-4066-5786-bafe-c3fdc96a06c9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Sums Over Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/id #uuid "8f09771b-3e0d-567b-a39f-f877bff53372" :question/math-academy-id "e-9481" :question/problem "Let $P = \\left\\{x_0, x_1, \\ldots, x_m\\right\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[-3, 4].$ If $\\Delta x_i = x_i - x_{i-1},$ calculate $\\displaystyle\\sum_{i=1}^m (x_i + x_{i-1})\\Delta x_i .$" :question/worked-solution "We can simplify the given summation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})Δ{x}_{1}+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})Δ{x}_{2}+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})Δ{x}_{m} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})({x}_{m}-{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})+({x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{m-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}}-{x}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}^{2}+{x}_{m}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $x_0 = -3$ and $x_m = 4$ are the endpoints of our partition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={4}^{2}-(-3)^{2} \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179585 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179723 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bc800b0-3901-5154-81ac-1ef853017320" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/id #uuid "eff8c72f-429d-583a-aa22-f7786f09262a" :question/math-academy-id "e-9484" :question/problem "Which of the following are partitions of the real interval $[1,9]?$\n\nI. $\\{1, 4, 5, 8\\}$\n\nII. $\\{1, 3, 4, 9\\}$\n\nIII. $1 <     2  <    9$" :question/worked-solution "A partition $P$ of a closed interval $[a,b]$ is a finite sequence of real numbers taken from $[a,b]$ such that\n\n$$\na = x_0 <      x_1<      x_2 <      \\ldots <      x_n = b\\,.\n$$\n\nWe can express $P$ using set notation as\n\n$$\nP=\\{x_0,x_1,\\ldots,x_n\\}.\n$$\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- Statement I is not a partition of $[1,9]$ since it does not include the right endpoint $b=9.$\n\n- Statement II is a partition of $[1,9].$\n\n- Statement III is a partition of $[1,9].$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179974 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179720 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c91d51f-39b4-547a-971b-9c2dada9eb47" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Simple Sums Over Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5452a419-f554-5118-a23f-5cda88d07a6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254406} {:answer/id #uuid "69cb96ae-4abe-536d-bbfd-27cb0e75035c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254621} {:answer/id #uuid "8befe275-f795-5d85-96a0-a058bfce5798" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254906} {:answer/id #uuid "c3345070-2312-5403-990f-8c38d4dd8121" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255413} {:answer/id #uuid "d9e4ca0a-0fab-5807-a6cc-43b4c721a0ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255603}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9e4ca0a-0fab-5807-a6cc-43b4c721a0ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255603} :answer-field/id #uuid "140841aa-de52-55f0-8588-33e4afa8583a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255954}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bd1432fb-079c-5b39-aa64-1524227d0162" :question/math-academy-id "q-122848" :question/problem "Let $P=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[0,3].$ If $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}5Δ{x}_{i}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple rule, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}5Δ{x}_{i}=5{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}$ is just the length of the interval $[0,3],$ because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})+({x}_{3}-{x}_{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}-{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}}-{x}_{0})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}})+(\\cancel{{x}_{3}}-\\cancel{{x}_{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}+{x}_{m} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}-{x}_{0} \\\\  & =3-0 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n5{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}=5\\cdot 3=15.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179975 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179721 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f55bdc9-4066-5786-bafe-c3fdc96a06c9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Sums Over Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29baeff2-fc72-53fa-9693-cdc59cdd0aba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254042} {:answer/id #uuid "629dd0b2-c1fa-5e1f-859d-1c6d8b40df77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254554} {:answer/id #uuid "8c488760-437b-50b1-a345-eceee411ae68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254912} {:answer/id #uuid "90d7b6c5-f82b-5d31-8429-6984ccaff8a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254942} {:answer/id #uuid "a7e14c1b-dcd3-580e-9613-3b51e5c5bdb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255151}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90d7b6c5-f82b-5d31-8429-6984ccaff8a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254942} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8ed8603-61d6-55f9-80ac-d3be0df34800" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256333}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3d3d4439-66c9-5ffc-a015-2454a6d340fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-122849" :question/problem "Let $P=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[0,2].$ If $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}.$" :question/worked-solution "We can simplify the given summation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})Δ{x}_{1}+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})Δ{x}_{2}+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})Δ{x}_{n} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})({x}_{m}-{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})+({x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{m-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}}-{x}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}^{2}+{x}_{m}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${x}_{0}=0$ and ${x}_{m}=2$ are the endpoints of our partition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={2}^{2}-{0}^{2} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179976 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179723 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bc800b0-3901-5154-81ac-1ef853017320" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b728c5ad-8596-577f-b670-49ffcac95099" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177526} {:answer/id #uuid "c7bcbcc5-8a88-5065-9d5f-5f895561daaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177527} {:answer/id #uuid "113bde06-2367-5118-9ad2-954102b4c31c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177528} {:answer/id #uuid "36a7a1f5-d6d4-5cb0-8dda-4bde93389735" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177530} {:answer/id #uuid "eb4418cf-cb76-5ba5-8c96-25fcc0a22bab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the statements give a partition of $[1,8]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523745}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b728c5ad-8596-577f-b670-49ffcac95099" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177526} :answer-field/id #uuid "08b74d7c-dacb-56bb-92c4-735bc234302a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177525}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7ab45c0e-0c7c-5664-9875-fc74cbb23147" :question/math-academy-id "q-122861" :question/problem "Which of the following are partitions of the real interval $[1,8]?$\n\nI. $1<2<4<8$\n\nII. $\\{1,3,4,8\\}$\n\nIII. $\\{2,4,8\\}$" :question/worked-solution "A partition $P$ of a closed interval $[a,b]$ is a finite sequence of real numbers taken from $[a,b]$ such that\n\n$$\na={x}_{0}<{x}_{1}<{x}_{2}<…<{x}_{n}=b\\,.\n$$\n\nWe can express $P$ using set notation as\n\n$$\nP=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{n}\\}.\n$$\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- Statement I is a partition of $[1,8].$\n\n- Statement II is a partition of $[1,8].$\n\n- Statement III is not a partition of $[1,8]$ since it does not include the left endpoint $a=1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523978 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179723 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bc800b0-3901-5154-81ac-1ef853017320" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4650d883-0024-5fb8-8a3b-926b85faeb7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523398} {:answer/id #uuid "91e31bb5-4dda-578c-be6e-626d6d5b43b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523560} {:answer/id #uuid "962aff86-8fb7-5334-ab89-1ce2ce31f5a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the statements give a partition of $[4,8]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523570} {:answer/id #uuid "99d35ace-ff4e-55ea-8ebe-8efeba21fc3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523574} {:answer/id #uuid "a79fcbcd-1c42-57fb-8ad9-6ece2081ead7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523607}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "99d35ace-ff4e-55ea-8ebe-8efeba21fc3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523574} :answer-field/id #uuid "97615891-a50f-5ff1-b957-2fefa73efcae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523868}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "84a42ed7-7cdb-52df-a889-40521b20e8c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-122930" :question/problem "Which of the following are partitions of the real interval $[4,8]?$\n\nI. $4<6<8$\n\nII. $5<6<7<8$\n\nIII. $4<5<6<7$" :question/worked-solution "A partition $P$ of a closed interval $[a,b]$ is a finite sequence of real numbers taken from $[a,b]$ such that\n\n$$\na={x}_{0}<{x}_{1}<{x}_{2}<…<{x}_{n}=b\\,.\n$$\n\nWe can express $P$ using set notation as\n\n$$\nP=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{n}\\}.\n$$\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- Statement I is a partition of $[4,8].$\n\n- Statement II is not a partition of $[4,8]$ since it does not include the left endpoint $a=4.$\n\n- Statement III is not a partition of $[4,8]$ since it does not include the right endpoint $b=8.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524022 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179723 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bc800b0-3901-5154-81ac-1ef853017320" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15b01046-18e1-58bb-9aae-addee4a5482b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523302} {:answer/id #uuid "79640bcf-217a-5e27-aca2-3c90383899ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523502} {:answer/id #uuid "84c6b261-478a-5a3c-8af3-eb635d34e070" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II  only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523534} {:answer/id #uuid "9e84a909-3d25-5602-9873-2133f303f3b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the statements give a partition of $[0,6]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523585} {:answer/id #uuid "cc89bb28-0e81-56bc-b07d-003f53e45ba1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523680}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15b01046-18e1-58bb-9aae-addee4a5482b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523302} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b6f0340-20ad-55e8-b95b-71619bc5062f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523811}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e49f5076-911d-5cdf-8140-a000de972953" :question/math-academy-id "q-122934" :question/problem "Which of the following are partitions of the real interval $[0,6]?$\n\nI. $0<2<4<8$\n\nII. $\\{0,3,6\\}$\n\nIII. $0<1<3<5<6$" :question/worked-solution "A partition $P$ of a closed interval $[a,b]$ is a finite sequence of real numbers taken from $[a,b]$ such that\n\n$$\na={x}_{0}<{x}_{1}<{x}_{2}<…<{x}_{n}=b\\,.\n$$\n\nWe can express $P$ using set notation as\n\n$$\nP=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{n}\\}.\n$$\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- Statement I is not a partition of $[0,6]$ since $8$ does not belong to $[0,6].$\n\n- Statement II is a partition of $[0,6].$\n\n- Statement III is a partition of $[0,6].$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256749 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179723 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bc800b0-3901-5154-81ac-1ef853017320" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26715d5c-8967-5870-a32d-f0e7de04504e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462097} {:answer/id #uuid "cffe34d1-2420-5409-9740-ce2cb5bd06e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462098}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26715d5c-8967-5870-a32d-f0e7de04504e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462097} :answer-field/id #uuid "59a63827-ba0c-5262-83e4-7514a1d6d98a" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462802} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5500db0b-5028-5ca1-9101-be045fa07fbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462099} {:answer/id #uuid "f59f0c27-693f-5b74-9c2c-1f1aaecba22c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462100}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5500db0b-5028-5ca1-9101-be045fa07fbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462099} :answer-field/id #uuid "4bd4fdc7-a23b-54cd-bd68-59ae2ea9f1c1" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462803} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bfc8220c-0f8b-58d7-84b9-a08eddb6eba8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462101} {:answer/id #uuid "646e11a8-a44c-5fe3-934b-ea14c43adefb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462102}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "646e11a8-a44c-5fe3-934b-ea14c43adefb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462102} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e42328f-21c1-5e9f-b9f3-96c9ef90effe" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462804}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bede805a-096d-538b-aca7-d4841b6beb80" :question/math-academy-id "q-122937" :question/problem "Which of the following are partitions of the real interval $[-3,7]?$\n- **I.** ${-3,-5,1,2,6}$\n- **II.** ${-3,0,3,7,8}$\n- **III.** ${-3,-2,1,3,4,7}$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A partition $P$ of a closed interval $[a,b]$ is a finite sequence of real numbers taken from $[a,b]$ such that\n\n$$\na={x}_{0}<{x}_{1}<{x}_{2}<…<{x}_{n}=b\\,.\n$$\n\nWe can express $P$ using set notation as\n\n$$\nP={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- Statement I is not a partition of $[-3,7]$ since it does not include the right endpoint $b=7.$\n\n- Statement II is not a partition of $[-3,7]$ since $8$ does not belong to $[-3,7].$\n\n- Statement III is a partition of $[-3,7].$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256750 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179723 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bc800b0-3901-5154-81ac-1ef853017320" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "72905ab0-a733-5444-b228-2909f22d66b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462103} {:answer/id #uuid "0bba932b-ac60-5190-b246-809450ca8184" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462104}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72905ab0-a733-5444-b228-2909f22d66b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462103} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9bcd569-770e-5e56-999c-b6c6fea7c704" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462805} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e8fceca-ad1f-553f-b1ae-fe2c3ddb4eab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462105} {:answer/id #uuid "882459bb-e603-5cca-bca5-49e509a1cc37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462106}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e8fceca-ad1f-553f-b1ae-fe2c3ddb4eab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462105} :answer-field/id #uuid "83c1ee2c-3ed9-508e-85bf-38d31fb14d69" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462806} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4bfb0fa3-fc7f-5f90-b747-7ae59892eded" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462107} {:answer/id #uuid "17db6afa-0a52-5a1b-b581-fb1c6a16a12b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462108}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "17db6afa-0a52-5a1b-b581-fb1c6a16a12b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462108} :answer-field/id #uuid "ecabc5c1-9328-5f82-a212-4432161d262a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462807}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8952dce8-c604-5674-b4ed-f948b3d55e92" :question/math-academy-id "q-122938" :question/problem "Which of the following are partitions of the real interval $[0,4]?$\n- **I.** $0<0.5<1.5<2.5<4<4.5$\n- **II.** ${0,1,2,3.9}$\n- **III.** $0<0.1<1.5<2.5<4$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A partition $P$ of a closed interval $[a,b]$ is a finite sequence of real numbers taken from $[a,b]$ such that\n\n$$\na={x}_{0}<{x}_{1}<{x}_{2}<…<{x}_{n}=b\\,.\n$$\n\nWe can express $P$ using set notation as\n\n$$\nP={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- Statement I is not a partition of $[0,4]$  since $4.5$ does not belong to $[0,4].$\n\n- Statement II is not a partition of $[0,4]$  since it does not include the left endpoint $a=4.$\n\n- Statement III is  a partition of  $[0,4].$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523942 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179720 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c91d51f-39b4-547a-971b-9c2dada9eb47" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Simple Sums Over Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6dbdbd0b-c1a2-51c0-a8f5-15cb04158568" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523478} {:answer/id #uuid "929a1813-87ee-5a94-b302-53b3394322ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523562} {:answer/id #uuid "960de9e7-c3d1-548d-bb28-aea79c7b0d3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523569} {:answer/id #uuid "d15c5ee3-1df2-5a89-801e-42aef64a0cac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523696} {:answer/id #uuid "d6c61e9b-6f94-5835-aa08-0cb0ef8d2485" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523707}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6dbdbd0b-c1a2-51c0-a8f5-15cb04158568" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523478} :answer-field/id #uuid "da6d1a46-d11c-5863-8635-3e515e9d04b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523898}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "28824d9b-0c0b-596c-9f64-75c745081e48" :question/math-academy-id "q-122969" :question/problem "Let $P=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[2,8].$ If $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}.$" :question/worked-solution "Note that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}$ is just the length of the interval $[2,8],$ because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})+({x}_{3}-{x}_{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}-{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}}-{x}_{0})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}})+(\\cancel{{x}_{3}}-\\cancel{{x}_{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}+{x}_{m} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}-{x}_{0} \\\\  & =8-2 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524036 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179720 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c91d51f-39b4-547a-971b-9c2dada9eb47" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Simple Sums Over Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07195f6c-4e48-5dcc-aec2-5d69c56026d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523272} {:answer/id #uuid "5665712a-009d-5af0-a804-20166b15f257" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523431} {:answer/id #uuid "916a6352-92eb-5096-b435-cd193b6feb37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523558} {:answer/id #uuid "f878e57d-c65e-5d5e-8918-ff905b1034b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523775} {:answer/id #uuid "ff90e828-6c3f-5567-ad48-f5f15d008572" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523787}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07195f6c-4e48-5dcc-aec2-5d69c56026d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523272} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ee43f80-f80a-52f4-830f-025c4b4ca95b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523796}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f1ddbd77-4be4-59b3-aa0d-217f8714ae20" :question/math-academy-id "q-122971" :question/problem "Let $P=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[-5,5].$ If $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}.$" :question/worked-solution "Note that ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}$ is just the length of the interval $[-5,5],$ because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j} & =({y}_{1}-{y}_{0})+({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})+({y}_{3}-{y}_{2})+⋯+({y}_{n}-{y}_{n-1}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{y}_{1}}-{y}_{0})+(\\cancel{{y}_{2}}-\\cancel{{y}_{1}})+(\\cancel{{y}_{3}}-\\cancel{{y}_{2}})+⋯+({y}_{n}-\\cancel{{y}_{n-1}}) \\\\  & =-{y}_{0}+{y}_{n} \\\\  & ={y}_{n}-{y}_{0} \\\\  & =5-(-5) \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256761 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179720 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c91d51f-39b4-547a-971b-9c2dada9eb47" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Simple Sums Over Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id 